WEBVTT

NOTE week06-clip3-linear-probing
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.267 line:2 align:center
Now we test what pretraining learned.
Take the pretrained encoder and freeze it,

2
00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:08.150 line:2 align:center
so none of its weights can change.

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.670 line:2 align:center
We need only a small labeled dataset.

4
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:19.483 line:2 align:center
Here, each ECG is labeled either atrial
fibrillation, AF, or normal sinus rhythm.

5
00:00:19.683 --> 00:00:25.109 line:2 align:center
The frozen encoder maps each ECG
to an embedding of 256 numbers.

6
00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:29.883 line:2 align:center
We draw these embeddings as
points in two dimensions.

7
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:33.547 line:2 align:center
On top, we add a single
linear prediction head.

8
00:00:33.547 --> 00:00:37.675 line:2 align:center
It computes a weighted sum
of the embedding plus a bias,

9
00:00:37.675 --> 00:00:42.217 line:2 align:center
and a sigmoid turns that
into the probability of AF.

10
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:47.437 line:2 align:center
During training, gradients flow into
the head only. The encoder is frozen,

11
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:50.017 line:2 align:center
so its weights never change.

12
00:00:50.217 --> 00:00:53.855 line:2 align:center
If one straight line can
separate AF from normal,

13
00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:57.086 line:2 align:center
the information was
already in the embedding.

14
00:00:57.086 --> 00:01:00.417 line:2 align:center
The head only has to read it out.

15
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:05.042 line:2 align:center
With fine-tuning, every weight is
trainable, including the encoder.

16
00:01:05.042 --> 00:01:08.984 line:2 align:center
A linear probe trains only 257 weights,

17
00:01:08.984 --> 00:01:14.083 line:2 align:center
so it measures what the pretrained
encoder already learned.

18
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:20.613 line:2 align:center
The same linear probe works for pathology.
A frozen encoder embeds each H&E tile,

19
00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:25.413 line:2 align:center
and a single linear head separates
tumor from normal mucosa.
